---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="First session"
  description="Install Veasel Code, connect a provider with /connect, and complete your first reviewed session."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / FIRST SESSION</p>
    <h1>
      From install to
      <br />
      <em>first review.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Four steps: install, connect, open a workspace, review before anything
      writes or runs.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>1. Install</h2>
      <p>
        Get a verified preview from the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/install/`}>install guide</a> or{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/downloads/`}>downloads</a>. Confirm with{" "}
        <code>veasel --version</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>2. Connect a model</h2>
      <pre><code>veasel
# then in the TUI:
/connect</code></pre>
      <p>
        <code>/connect</code> is the happy path: paste an API key when needed,
        save it on this machine, and pick a model. For endpoint and
        output-budget controls, press <kbd>s</kbd> or use <code>/models</code>{" "}
        (Ctrl+U / Ctrl+O). Local presets such as Ollama do not need a key.
        Choosing a model saves the provider profile. Zero output budget keeps
        Veasel’s 4,096-token default, except Meta, which omits the field so Meta
        applies its own limit.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>3. Open a workspace session</h2>
      <p>
        Create or select a session bound to an existing project directory.
        Messages and events store in local SQLite. On the home screen,{" "}
        <kbd>j</kbd>/<kbd>k</kbd> (or arrows) move, type to filter, <kbd>1</kbd>
        –<kbd>9</kbd> jump labeled slots, and Enter opens. Ask a question about
        the repo — Veasel may request bounded list/read/search tools inside that
        root. Full shortcuts live in the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/tui/`}>TUI guide</a> and <code>/help</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>4. Review before effect</h2>
      <p>
        Default policy is <code>ask</code>: proposals do not change the
        workspace until you inspect and approve. Opt-in{" "}
        <code>auto-edit</code> / <code>sandbox-auto</code> (server env gates)
        can auto-apply edits or sandboxed shell — see{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>security</a>. Interactive review:
      </p>
      <pre><code>/patches
/patch show &lt;id&gt;
/patch approve &lt;id&gt;

/commands
/command show &lt;id&gt;
/command approve &lt;id&gt;

/mcp add [user|project] stdio &lt;name&gt; &lt;command&gt; [args…]
/mcp trust configured/&lt;name&gt;
/mcp calls
/mcp call approve &lt;id&gt;</code></pre>
      <p>
        Diff reviews lead with add/remove line counts. Shell reviews show the
        exact command, working directory, timeout, and whether a platform
        sandbox will wrap the process. MCP needs per-session trust plus per-call
        argument review (user/project config or portable <code>.mcp.json</code>
        ). For Streamable HTTP auth, use named credentials, TUI{" "}
        <code>/mcp oauth authorize|complete</code>, or headless{" "}
        <code>veasel mcp oauth … --listen</code> (prints the authorize URL; no
        automatic browser launch — see the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>MCP guide</a>). Interrupted or
        rejected work is not replayed automatically.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Know the boundary.</strong> Session history stays local; prompts
      and tool excerpts go to your configured provider. Approved shell uses
      Bubblewrap / Seatbelt / Windows AppContainer+Job when available — best
      effort, not a VM. MCP stays unsandboxed. Read the{" "}
      <a href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>security notes</a> before sensitive
      work.
    </aside>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/tui/`}>
        Learn the TUI <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>
        More providers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/mcp/`}>
        MCP servers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
